@startuml qnx_dispatch_engine_dispatch_activity
title DispatchThreadRunner - worker-thread dispatch

start
:Enter the worker lambda launched by StartPostInit();
:Acquire and release thread_mutex_\nStartup releases it after assigning thread_ and restoring the caller mask;
:Enter RunOnThread();
while (quit_flag_ is false?) is (yes)
    if (dispatch_block(context_pointer_) succeeds?) then (yes)
        :dispatch_handler(context_pointer_)\nInvoke registered callbacks on this worker thread;
        note right
            Both runners: QuitPulseCallback sets quit_flag_.
            Client runner: timer, select and connection-death pulses.
            Server runner: resource-manager connect/I/O callbacks.
        end note
        :Ignore the dispatch_handler result;
    else (error)
        :Retry the dispatch loop;
    endif
endwhile (no)
:Return from RunOnThread and the worker lambda;
stop

legend
    All actions here run on one runner's background thread.
    There are separate client and server instances of this activity.
    Start and Stop execute on their callers, in the separate lifecycle view.
    The Stop caller joins this worker before freeing its context and buffers.
endlegend

@enduml
